    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all 3 tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store and compare numbers in E.164 form.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced the \"strip non-digits, require exactly 10\" logic with a `toE164(String)` helper that:\n- strips spaces, dashes and brackets (`[\\s\\-()]`);\n- keeps a leading `+` and country code when present; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits;\n- requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, returning `null` (\u2192 HTTP 400) when the number can't form valid E.164.\n\n`addOwner` now stores the E.164 string as `telephone` and detects duplicates by comparing E.164 values (normalizing each existing owner's number the same way).\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 the entity validation constraint was the source of a 500 (it forced exactly 10 digits). Replaced `@Digits(...)` + `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` with `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` and removed the now-unused `@Digits` import, so the persisted E.164 value validates.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `telephone` field description and example (`+61412345678`) to document the new normalization; the DTO carried no pattern constraint, so nothing else needed changing.\n\nVerified behavior matches the spec/tests: `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`, and `12` \u2192 400. `./mvnw test`: **3 run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS.**",
